# Cross-engine comparison at 16 policies, mutating half only.
#
# The selectors variant is required here, and it is the default below. With
# matchConditions each policy gets its own webhook, mutating webhooks run in
# sequence over the progressively patched object, and the
# annotation-not-already-present condition means only the first copy ever
# executes - about one execution per request instead of sixteen, so there is no
# per-request policy loop to measure.
#
# The selectors variant moves the add-only logic into the patch value, so all 16
# execute. Note what that means for realism: 15 of the 16 patches re-add a value
# that is already present. The engine still performs a full match, CEL evaluation
# and JSONPatch construction for each, and re-serializes the object between
# policies, so the engine cost is real - but a cluster running 16 mutating
# policies would have each of them change something different.
ENGINES=${ENGINES:-"baseline kyverno kyverno-cel gatekeeper native"}
POLICY_COUNT=${POLICY_COUNT:-16}
POLICY_MODE=${POLICY_MODE:-mutate}
KYVERNO_CEL_VARIANT=${KYVERNO_CEL_VARIANT:-selectors}
PAYLOAD_PROFILE=${PAYLOAD_PROFILE:-minimal}
TARGET_RPS=${TARGET_RPS:-200}
TRIALS=${TRIALS:-3}
PROFILE=${PROFILE:-scaling}
